            <ArticleTitle>[Postoperative oxadol analgesia in oncologic patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oxadol (nefopam hydrochloride), a central analgesic, was used for postoperative pain relief in patients operated on the abdominal and pelvic organs for cancer. The analgesic effect of oxadol was sufficient for arresting moderate postoperative pain. Although the drug exerts rather many side effects, none of them notably deteriorated the clinical status of patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
